Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||10:04 PM||||Boy I sure would hate to change them back plugs ||||reg||1
Z||000004||AkursedX||08-29-2001||11:45 PM||||I have seen this done before.  There is a guy who lives about 2 minutes from me that has one Fiero done like this, and he is working on 2 more.  The engine is longitudinally mounted, and it adds alot of weight to the rear end (about 300lbs I was told)  I am sure this effects handling alot, so if I were to do this, I would go with coil-overs and a higher spring rate, like 375lbs or so, to handle the heavier weight.<P>As for the cradle, he welded the front of a Fiero cradle to the Toronado frame.<P>So yes, it can be done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||08-30-2001||07:33 AM||||The Fiero in my sig.has the Toronado 425A transmission coupled to a small block.Unless you flip the rear(which I've never done)you will have too much weight hanging behind the rear wheels.My car weighs 3400 lbs.2200 on the rear and 1200 on the front.I'm changing to the 3800SC so I can get the handling back to where it should be.The Toronado drivetrain will be for sale when the swap is done. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/hugh_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||TONY_C||08-30-2001||09:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>The Fiero in my sig.has the Toronado 425A transmission coupled to a small block.Unless you flip the rear(which I've never done)you will have too much weight hanging behind the rear wheels.My car weighs 3400 lbs.2200 on the rear and 1200 on the front.I'm changing to the 3800SC so I can get the handling back to where it should be.The Toronado drivetrain will be for sale when the swap is done. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Hugh, How do you "flip" the rear?  do you know?  do you know anyone who has?  <BR>TIA, hope you can shed some light on this topic.<BR>Tony<P>||||reg||1
